[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186129154,
      "id": "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443",
      "title": "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "40f8bb9d-c389-54e1-8158-e8eebc54a5fc",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/4604d597342b336b42d1edae7cf9089f7736f7d524643f9ebd968f2fe034586c.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=1$ is a simple root.\n- **II.** $x=4$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n- **III.** $x=4$ is a simple root.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=1$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=4$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=4$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=4$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at that point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
