    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ad8d2cf5-eb13-53a8-ae28-4b420af6ea6f",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/a263d6162360d5b0f9a727a27d5a70a94e878335e9e5934035f48e5c1294d26e.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x = 0$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n- **II.** $x =-3$ and $x = 2$ are roots of even multiplicity.\n- **III.** $p(x) \u2192 \u221e$ as $x \u2192 \u221e$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The graph crosses at x=0 (odd multiplicity) and touches/turns at x=-3 and x=2 (even multiplicities). Its right-hand tail rises, giving p(x) tending to positive infinity.",
