  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186129154,
      "id": "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443",
      "title": "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7dd2baa6-0bbb-5f03-8214-1aae7be66cbc",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/bbbb90c144f078892bf6c9fbf7aa1365d5b85c5c486b3da0d6810b13f1245d59.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=4$ is a simple root.\n\n- **II.** $x=1$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n\n- **III.** $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=4$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=1$  has an even multiplicity because at $x=1$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement III is false. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves up in the positive direction towards $+\\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e7e5475a-b78e-5cdc-986e-b052677f91f5",
