      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/94aca6ac8c6a42b84eb7bfea80d9f9d70ea8b619c0589a28a2ad76403970199d.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x = 5$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n- **II.** $x = \u00b1 2$ are roots of odd multiplicity.\n- **III.** $p(0) = 2$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "At x=5 the curve touches and turns at the x-axis (even multiplicity). At x=-2 and x=2 it crosses (odd multiplicity). The y-intercept is below zero, so p(0)=2 is false.",
