    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e7b09dec-4ae9-5123-bafb-a1a6a4438baa",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/bd96c5e928b2e036516a34b29c0d506a53da2455837997e470c05362233bbe86.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x = 2$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n- **II.** $x = \u00b1 1$ are roots of odd multiplicity.\n- **III.** $p(0) = 2$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "At x=2 the curve touches and turns at the x-axis (even multiplicity). At x=-1 and x=1 it crosses (odd multiplicity). The y-intercept is below zero, so p(0)=2 is false.",
